    <briefdescription>
<para>Selects the coarsest downsampling tier that satisfies a query&apos;s resolution. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Given a requested query window width (the granularity the caller wants data at), <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_tier_selector" kindref="compound">TierSelector</ref> returns the tier whose resolution is ≤ requested_resolution with the largest window size, i.e. the coarsest tier that still provides the required detail.</para>
<para>This is typically invoked by <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_t_s_query_optimizer" kindref="compound">TSQueryOptimizer</ref> to route aggregate reads to the smallest-data-volume tier. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
